   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to removing residency\nrequirements for Washington county deputy county attorneys",
    "basePrintNo": "S10162",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10162-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 45,
       "fullName": "Dan Stec",
       "imgName": "674_dan_stec.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1490,
       "sessionMemberId": 2362,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "STEC"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10162\n\nSPONSOR: ASHBY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to removing resi-\ndency requirements for Washington county deputy county attorneys\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo remove residency requirements for Washington county deputy county\nattorneys\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 states that In the county of Washington, the provisions\nrequiring a person to be a resident of the political subdivision or\nmunicipal corporation of the state for which such person shall be chosen\nor within which such person's official functions are required to be\nexercised, shall not prevent a person from holding the office of the\ndeputy county attorney of the county of Washington, provided that such\nperson resides in Washington county or an adjoining county within the\nstate of New York; provided, however that any person performing such\nfunctions or holding the office of the deputy county attorney in any\nother county shall be a resident of such county unless otherwise\nprovided by law.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date to immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Washington County Board of Supervisors, on behalf of the County of\nWashington, requested that the NYS Legislature enact legislation allow-\ning Washington County to hire a Deputy County Attorney who resides in a\ncontiguous county to Washington County.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
